One <100> dumbbell in an fcc crystal.

  sh insert.sh     builds a 10 x 10 x 10 fcc cell (4000 atoms) and inserts the
                   dumbbell at site (2,2,2): 4001 atoms in formd_new.str
  sh clean.sh      removes the files produced by the run

The fcc counterpart of 001_SIA_110: cube.x is given option 1 (fcc) and
put_vct.x the defect type 3. Sites in fcc have an even sum of indices. To
change the cell, the sites or the defect type, edit the three short blocks of
insert.sh. Keep the lattice parameter at 2.8553.

The crystal is built with the bcc lattice parameter of the code; rescale the
result to the lattice parameter of the fcc metal you want, as explained in
doc/concepts.md.
